# Shell scripts must stay LF in the working tree on every platform. A CRLF
# checkout produces a script bash refuses to run, and plugins/spk/templates/
# ships its contents to users.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Markdown must stay LF too. The retained upstream mirrors under docs/ are
# gated on a sha256 of their content, and Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true — a CRLF checkout rewrites every byte and failed all 25
# pages while macOS and Linux passed. The gate normalises line endings when it
# reads, so this rule is the second layer, not the only one.
*.md text eol=lf
